=== entry 0b0322c7b2d6
kind: translation
rules: model-role, model-effort, general-purpose
intent: Runners come from the `arena runners` line in the project models file, else willyskills's default, applied with the model-entry snippet; the agent type, the rejected-slug and family-prefix fallbacks, and the reasoning-level sentence are dropped. Preserve the frame steps, the more-runners and repeat-one-model guidance, and the per-candidate output location.
--- upstream
1. State the artifact each candidate is producing.
2. Derive the rubric, 3-6 concrete gradeable criteria for what success looks like on *this* task. It is the picker's tool in Phase D. Candidates only see the task.
3. Pick the runners from the `arena runners` line in `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`, by default `claude-fable-5-2-high`, `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast`, and `gemini-4-carbon-high`. An `auto` or `inherit-parent` entry is the parent model, so omit `model` and spawn `generalPurpose`. If the Task tool rejects a slug, use the nearest valid slug of the same family or drop the seat, keep at least two runners, and say so. Families go by prefix, and the longest match wins: `claude-fable-*`, `claude-*`, and `gemini-*`, after dropping a leading `cursor-`. Any other slug's family is its text before the first hyphen. Spawn more for multiple design directions, and repeat one model when the work is generation-bound, not judgment-sensitive. Pick each subagent's reasoning level per the Subagents section of the **poteto-mode** skill.
4. Give each candidate its own output location (a git worktree where possible, otherwise `/tmp/arena-<slug>/candidate-<n>/`), per the **separate-before-serializing-shared-state** principle skill.
--- patched
1. State the artifact each candidate is producing.
2. Derive the rubric, 3-6 concrete gradeable criteria for what success looks like on *this* task. It is the picker's tool in Phase D. Candidates only see the task.
3. Pick the runners from the `arena runners` line in {{snippet:models-file}}, else {{model:arena runners}}, one runner per entry. {{snippet:model-entry}} Spawn more for multiple design directions, and repeat one model when the work is generation-bound, not judgment-sensitive.
4. Give each candidate its own output location (a git worktree where possible, otherwise `/tmp/arena-<slug>/candidate-<n>/`), per the **separate-before-serializing-shared-state** principle skill.

=== entry d37e705c0111
kind: translation
rules: model-role, delegate, read-only, background, same-model-review
intent: The judge is a read-only async delegate_task child from the `arena cross-judge pool` line in the project models file, else willyskills's default. It takes the first entry whose provider differs from the parent's, else the first entry, so a judge always runs even when the pool holds one provider (as setup-pstack describes the pool). The Fable-is-Claude note, the unknown-parent note and the rejected-slug fallbacks are dropped with model-role. Preserve that it starts after all candidates complete and scores each by path label on each criterion while you read in Phase D.
--- upstream
After all Phase B candidates complete, spawn one readonly judge from the `arena cross-judge pool` line in `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`, by default `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast`, `gemini-4-carbon-high`. The judge is never from the parent's vendor, and Fable counts as Claude for that check, so use the first entry from another vendor. An `auto` or `inherit-parent` entry is the parent model. If you do not know the parent's model, use the first real slug and say that the vendor check did not run. If the Task tool rejects a slug, use the nearest valid slug of the same family, then the next such entry, or skip the judge, and say so. While you read in Phase D, the judge scores each candidate, by path label, on each rubric criterion and recommends a base.
--- patched
After all Phase B candidates complete, spawn one judge from the `arena cross-judge pool` line in {{snippet:models-file}}, else {{model:arena cross-judge pool}}: the first entry whose provider differs from the parent's (`orchestrator_capabilities` gives the parent's), else the first entry. An `inherit-parent` entry is the parent's model, so it never counts as another provider. Spawn it with `delegate_task`, `mode: "async"`, and no `isolation`. Its brief says "Do not edit, create, commit, or push files.", and you run `git status` afterward. While you read in Phase D, the judge scores each candidate, by path label, on each rubric criterion and recommends a base.
